Hi all,

I have a question about the scantwo summary output:
does anyone have an explanation why R reports me p-values of 1 and 0 for the lod.int <http://lod.int> and lod.add output? This looks rather strange to me...

scan2_hk_summary <- summary(result_scan2_hk, perms = perm_scan2_hk, alpha = 0.2, pvalues=T)

                pos1f pos2f lod.full pval lod.fv1 pval lod.int <http://lod.int> pval
cs12916:cs13340 92.16  74.1     10.1 0.03    4.86 0.99    1.63    1

pos1a  pos2a lod.add pval lod.av1 pval
92.16   80.1     8.5    0    3.23 0.19

Thank you very much in advance for your comments!

Cheers,

Anna

From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Mon Sep 10 14:45:27 2018
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Mon, 10 Sep 2018 14:45:27 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] funny scantwo p-values
Message-ID: <GtPiOQctmw0.QPin1yOjFQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <GtPiOQctmw0.wSfEsuSaFQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <GtPiOQctmw0.wSfEsuSaFQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/GtPiOQctmw0/m/QPin1yOjFQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The p-values are the proportion of permutation replicates with LOD scores >= the observed.
So if no permutations gave that big of a LOD score, the p-value will be 0.
If all permutations gave that big of a LOD score, the p-value will be 1.

karl

